<%- include('partials/head') %>
<%- include('partials/header') %>

<main>
  <section class="section" style="padding-bottom:0">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="kicker">The rules, written down</span>
      <h1 style="margin:0.9rem 0 1rem">How booking works</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Availability is the part of a travel site people get lied to about most, so
        here is exactly what happens between you clicking a date and a seat being
        yours.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="itin" style="max-width:62rem">
        <div class="itin__row" id="live">
          <div class="itin__day">Step 01</div>
          <div>
            <div class="itin__t">The calendar reads live inventory</div>
            <p class="itin__b">
              Every date is answered from the database when the page loads, again when
              you change month, again when you come back to the tab, and once more
              every minute you leave it open. A departure that fills while you are
              reading the itinerary turns grey in front of you, with a note saying so.
              Nothing on this site is served from a cached seat count.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="itin__row" id="holds">
          <div class="itin__day">Step 02</div>
          <div>
            <div class="itin__t">Choosing a date holds the seats for <%= holdMinutes %> minutes</div>
            <p class="itin__b">
              The hold is taken before the payment form is shown, not after. That is
              the whole point: you should never be asked for a card for a seat that
              someone else is in the middle of buying. The clock is visible on the
              checkout page. If it runs out the seats go straight back to the pool and
              nothing is charged — we would rather release a seat than sell it twice.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="itin__row">
          <div class="itin__day">Step 03</div>
          <div>
            <div class="itin__t">The last seat can only be sold once</div>
            <p class="itin__b">
              The final seat increment is guarded inside the database transaction
              itself — the write simply will not apply if it would push a departure
              past its capacity. If two payments arrived in the same instant, one
              succeeds and the other is told before any money moves. This is belt and
              braces on top of the hold, and it is the reason we can print a real
              number instead of “limited availability”.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="itin__row" id="deposits">
          <div class="itin__day">Step 04</div>
          <div>
            <div class="itin__t">Deposits and balances</div>
            <p class="itin__b">
              Adventure trips take a 30% deposit, city breaks 50%, and charters 25%,
              because that is roughly when we have to commit money to lodges, boats and
              crew. The balance is due 60 days before departure and we email a reminder
              at 74 days. Deposits are calculated in whole currency units — you will
              never see a bill ending in a stray fraction of a cent.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="itin__row">
          <div class="itin__day">Step 05</div>
          <div>
            <div class="itin__t">Online booking closes <%= cutoffDays %> days before departure</div>
            <p class="itin__b">
              After that the guide already has the manifest and the permits are filed,
              so late joiners are handled by hand rather than by form. Parties above
              <%= maxSeats %> travellers are also arranged off-site — a group that size
              changes the vehicle, the guide ratio and usually the price.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="itin__row" id="cancellation">
          <div class="itin__day">Step 06</div>
          <div>
            <div class="itin__t">If you cancel, or we do</div>
            <p class="itin__b">
              Cancel more than 60 days out and you lose the deposit only. Inside 60
              days the balance is non-refundable, which is what travel insurance is
              for — and insurance is a condition of joining any of the adventure
              departures. If <em>we</em> cancel a departure, for weather, permits or
              numbers, you get the full amount back including the deposit, or a
              transfer to any other date at the price you originally paid.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="notice notice--demo" style="max-width:62rem; margin-top:2rem">
        <span class="notice__i">i</span>
        <p>
          This is a demonstration build. The catalogue is illustrative, the payment
          gateway is a stand-in that cannot charge a real card, and the terms above
          are written as an example of the level of detail a real booking page needs —
          they are not a contract.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>

<%- include('partials/footer') %>
